1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:09,500
1818: Victor Frankenstein stitched the dead together with thread and lightning.

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:19,500
2026: biology does it with induced pluripotent stem cells.

3
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:34,500
Case 02, Ghost Heart: a dead heart stripped to a white scaffold,
re-seeded with cells until it beats.

4
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:44,500
Six real peer-reviewed experiments,
each with its journal, year and PubMed ID.

5
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:54,500
Ask anything. The lab checks Europe PMC and Wikipedia live
and shows its sources.

6
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:09,500
Design Room: stitch your own chimera.
A free AI image previews it first.

7
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:19,500
Every stat shares a 450-point budget.
No stat or win chance is ever 0% or 100%.

8
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:34,500
The bioreactor grows it through six stages as its heartbeat rises.

9
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:44,500
Then it breaks the glass and wakes up.

10
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:54,500
The arena: two monsters,
one 16-second AI battle written from their stats.

11
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:14,500
Fists, claws, tail, spinning kicks, a flame cannon,
and a laser-eye finisher.

12
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:24,500
Every battle gets its story; the Monster Manager
saves, renames and exports your monsters.

13
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:39,500
Built with Kiro: specs for every feature,
steering rules, and agent hooks.

14
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:49,500
398 tests, including property-based tests with fast-check.

15
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:55,000
PROMETHEUS-iPSC.
Has science already crossed Frankenstein's threshold?
